      "About this story": 1,
      "Illustrations are imaginative composites, not portraits or eyewitness scenes. Marina's story comes from Lebanese tradition, written down in later sources. Historians do not agree on when she lived, and the Orthodox Church tells a different version of the story, so this book gives no dates. The details about the milk and the monk who was blind in one eye are told as 'the old story says'. The last two pages mention modern times: a pilgrimage in 2018 and the chapel visitors can see today.": 1,
      "Frequently Asked Questions": 1,
      "Who was Saint Marina?": 1,
      "A woman remembered in Lebanese tradition as Marina the Monk, who lived as Brother Marinos at the Monastery of Qannoubine in the Qadisha Valley.": 1,
